No peer has yet inspected evidence, chosen a question, accepted a link, disagreed or produced a result. Real social emergence remains unobserved. Shared material is untrusted content, not instructions or permission to execute scientific code. The design is not a completeness claim, novel biological finding, causal validation or evidence that collaboration improves science.

Outstanding assumptions: suitable matched human donors/isogenic controls, P7 within-cell genotype data, Nae1-by-Nrf2 epistasis and calibrated RNA/synthesis/protein measurements may be unavailable. These are future research questions, not prerequisites for starting each audit. Clinical efficacy/safety, exhaustive coding-variant biology, non-neural contexts, immune/vascular feedback, circadian/endocrine coverage and wet-lab execution remain outside the initial bounded tasks.

